-- =============================================================================
-- Regenerate hierarchy views/TVFs + provision the MJ: Form Chrome Rules entity
-- =============================================================================
--
-- Pure CodeGen output. There is no hand-written DDL above it, because this migration
-- exists to APPLY generation the repo already shipped artifacts for but never shipped a
-- migration for. Precedent: V202510151145__v2.107.x__Regenerate_All_Views.sql.
--
-- WHY THIS IS NEEDED. IT50 (codegen-determinism CD3/CD5/CD6) compares the committed
-- generated TypeScript against live metadata on a database built from committed
-- migrations only. CI runs no live CodeGen, so anything the repo generates but does not
-- migrate shows up as drift. Two independent causes, both fixed here:
--
--   1. HIERARCHY (CD3). PR #3967 shipped metadata/entities/.entity-field-hierarchy-
--      configurations.json plus regenerated TypeScript, and no migration. CodeGen turns
--      that seed into per-field hierarchy TVFs and base-view lateral joins projecting
--      Root<Field>, <Field>Depth, <Field>Path, <Field>IsLeaf, <Field>ChildCount.
--      34 hierarchy fields across 34 entities; 136 new virtual EntityField rows.
--
--   2. MJ: FORM CHROME RULES (CD5/CD6). V202608151200__v6.1.x__Form_Chrome_Rules.sql
--      creates the table and states in a comment that CodeGen handles the Entity /
--      EntityField metadata "automatically". True for a developer who runs CodeGen;
--      false for CI and for any fresh install. The Entity row is inserted below, taking
--      the core entity count from 378 to the 379 the generated artifacts register.
--
-- TWO CODEGEN PASSES, CONCATENATED. Within a single pass CodeGen syncs EntityField
-- metadata BEFORE it regenerates views, so the virtual columns pass 1 creates are only
-- visible to the field sync on a SECOND pass. Pass 1 supplies views/TVFs and the Entity
-- row; pass 2 supplies the 136 EntityField rows describing pass 1's new view columns.
-- Both are required. Without pass 2 the base views expose more columns than the entities
-- declare, positional save-capture misaligns, every write to an affected entity fails,
-- and `mj sync push` -- a required CI step -- dies partway through.
--
-- DROPPED VIEW COLUMNS -- read before merging. The OLD CodeGen emitted a Root<Field>
-- column for ANY self-referencing FK; the NEW one emits it only for fields seeded
-- IsHierarchy=true. NINE Root* columns therefore leave the base views (43 -> 34 across
-- the schema, measured against a pre-PR baseline database):
--
--   RootConsolidatedIntoNoteID   RootDefaultCoAgentID       RootLastConversationID
--   RootLastRunID                RootLastSessionID          RootMergedIntoTagID
--   RootRerunFromPromptRunID     RootRestoredFromID         RootResultSelectorPromptID
--
-- None has an in-repo consumer (TypeScript, metadata or queries), and R__RefreshMetadata
-- removes their EntityField rows once the columns leave the views. But saved User Views,
-- ad-hoc queries and downstream OpenApps referencing them get "Invalid column name" with
-- no warning. Re-seeding any of these fields as IsHierarchy=true restores its Root column
-- and adds the four hierarchy columns alongside it.
--
-- APPLIES TO FRESH / MIGRATIONS-ONLY DATABASES. The Form Chrome Rules provisioning below
-- is CodeGen's unguarded "new entity" output: it assumes the Entity row and the
-- __mj_CreatedAt/__mj_UpdatedAt columns do not exist yet, which holds for CI, for fresh
-- installs, and for any database built from migrations alone (V202608151200 creates the
-- table but deliberately leaves that metadata to CodeGen). It does NOT hold on a dev box
-- that ran `mj codegen` locally after migrating next -- there it fails with "Column names
-- in each table must be unique". Accepted deliberately: v6.1.x is unreleased and the
-- table is days old, so that population is local dev databases only, each of which can
-- re-migrate from scratch.
--
-- NOT COVERED, deliberately: MJ: Employees.SupervisorID and MJ: Entities.ParentID. Both
-- are self-referencing FKs with single-column PKs, but both entities have
-- BaseViewGenerated = 0 (hand-written base views), so CodeGen has nowhere to project
-- hierarchy columns and skips them silently. Their seed entries are removed in this PR.
-- MJ: Employees is a candidate for the layered-base-view treatment
-- (V202608050105__v6.1.x__Layered_Base_Views_Pilot.sql); MJ: Entities is deliberately
-- excluded by that pilot, since vwEntities is what the metadata layer itself reads.
-- =============================================================================


